\newlabel{fig:chainbox}{{4}{11}{Distribution of longest AI$\to $AI chain length per PR, by quarter. Boxes show the interquartile range with whiskers at 1.5$\times $IQR. Fliers are omitted. Annotations report the quarterly mean and $p_{95}$. The tail grows monotonically: $p_{95}$ triples from 2025-Q2 to 2026-Q1 (share of PRs with chain $\geq $5 grew 8.8$\times $ over the same period). The single-PR maximum (13) is stable, indicating growth driven by more \emph {PRs} having long chains rather than any one PR having an unprecedentedly long chain}{figure.caption.9}{}}
\newlabel{fig:chainbox@cref}{{[figure][4][2147483647]4}{[1][10][]11}}
