\newlabel{fig:withinpr-native}{{5}{13}{Within-PR DiD on the dual-review cohort, with the AI opinion pool restricted to native \texttt {APPROVED} / \texttt {CHANGES\_REQUESTED} review states only (symmetric with the human side). Pooled across the full Apr 2025--Mar 2026 window: 85{} AI-authored and 4,609{} human-authored PRs. Same construction as Figure~\ref {fig:withinpr}. DiD $\widehat {\rbt ^A - \rbt ^H} = +4.60{}$~pp (95\% CI [-5.73, +14.94]{}) --- the headline negative result in \S \ref {sec:results} does not replicate in this small sample with only explicit review events included: the gap on AI-authored PRs is +1.18{}~pp [95\% CI [-9.11, +11.46]{}] vs.\ a gap of -3.43{}~pp [95\% CI [-4.49, -2.37]{}] on human-authored PRs, and the DiD's CI crosses zero}{figure.caption.10}{}}
\newlabel{fig:withinpr-native@cref}{{[figure][5][2147483647]5}{[1][13][]13}}
\newlabel{tab:rq3-quarterly}{{5}{14}{Within-PR DiD (\S \ref {sec:results}) by PR-creation quarter. Top panel: cross-family DiD on the stable doubly-engaged Any-AI-and-human cohort. Bottom panel: within-family DiD on the Claude-and-human cohort, with author restricted to Claude or human (the 2025-Q2 Claude-author cell is empty in the cohort, so its DiD is undefined). The gap on each author-side row is the AI-reviewer approval rate minus the human-reviewer approval rate (in pp); the DiD is the gap on AI-/Claude-authored PRs minus the gap on human-authored PRs. 95\% CIs are analytical (two independent gaps summed in quadrature on the rate-difference scale)}{table.caption.11}{}}
\newlabel{tab:rq3-quarterly@cref}{{[table][5][2147483647]5}{[1][13][]14}}
